To see activity on your timeline, tell RustMeter what you want to measure. The easiest way to do this is by adding the #[monitor_fn] attribute to a function. Note: Embassy Tasks will be automatically traced if you enabled the trace feature for embassy-executor, so you don't need to add any manual instrumentation to them. However, for other functions or specific code blocks, you can use the provided macros later in the guide. use rustmeter_beacon::monitor_fn;
use embassy_time::{Duration, Timer}; #[monitor_fn]
async fn my_monitored_time_spending() { // The total time spent in this function will be recorded Timer::after(Duration::from_millis(100)).await;
}

